# Build trees
build/
compile_commands.json

# Vendored third-party sources. Grammar trees are fetched by
# scripts/vendor.sh at pinned refs (recorded in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md),
# but KEEP the project-owned build glue: without third_party/CMakeLists.txt
# a fresh clone cannot configure. The OmniDecide-C kernel tree is COMMITTED
# by design (vendor decision L8, third_party/omnidecide/PROVENANCE.md):
# it is integrity-checked by scripts/vendor.sh against its committed
# VENDOR.sha256 manifest, not fetched.
third_party/*
!third_party/CMakeLists.txt
!third_party/omnidecide

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
__pycache__/

# Test scratch output
/tmp/
*.log
core
core.*
# EXCEPT the resolver-v3 fixture mypkg/core.py: its name matches the
# core-dump pattern above, so it silently stayed untracked and a fresh
# clone failed test_sprint4 (2/58). Caught by the M1 drift replay leg of
# the 2026-11-18 ritual dress rehearsal -- the fixture MUST be tracked.
!tests/fixtures_sprint4/pyabs/mypkg/core.py

# Local scratch (perf corpus etc.) -- generated by scripts/perf_gen.py, never committed
work/

# Release artifacts (regenerate with scripts/package.sh; evidence is the script + verdict JSON)
dist/

