ktor

# SPRINT-23 restore leg: `core.*` above silently untracked the Kotlin
# resolver fixture (files_analyzed 11 -> 10, test_sprint22 1 failure).
# Same landmine as the core.py exception above -- the fixture MUST be
# tracked. Caught by the 2026-11-23 slim-artifact restore on a degraded
# tree; the M1 drift-replay lesson applies to restores, not just clones.
!tests/fixtures/kotlin_resolver/core.kt

# SPRINT-25 restore legs (closed-loop fix wave):
# (a) the generated scala_resolver fixture core.scala matches `core.*`
# above; the sprint-24 archive shipped one generated Scala fixture short
# (audit note N-5) and a fresh restore re-lost it (test_sprint24 and
# test_sprint25 unit_n5_scala_fixtures_present both failed). The fixture
# MUST be tracked; gen_fixtures_scala.py remains its generator.
!tests/fixtures/scala_resolver/core.scala
# (b) the environment-level `node_modules/` ignore (project-root
# .gitignore, outside this repo) untracked the discovery fixture stubs:
# tests/fixtures/js/node_modules/skip.js ("discovery must never report
# it") and tests/fixtures_sprint2/dots/node_modules/dep.js (OBS-1
# files_skipped_ignored_dirs 1 -> 0, test_sprint2 1 failure). Same
# landmine class as the core.py/core.kt exceptions -- these fixtures
# MUST be tracked; only the named stubs are re-included.
!tests/fixtures/js/node_modules/
tests/fixtures/js/node_modules/*
!tests/fixtures/js/node_modules/skip.js
!tests/fixtures_sprint2/dots/node_modules/
tests/fixtures_sprint2/dots/node_modules/*
!tests/fixtures_sprint2/dots/node_modules/dep.js

